# The `ai` image: the sentiment worker. No database driver needed.
-r base.in
# Security floors (Task 2.6, see docs/security.md); `make lock` picks the newest
# release above them. Any change here must pass scripts/sentiment_golden.py --check.
# torch is pinned exactly: on Linux the `+cpu` build exists only on PyTorch's
# CPU index, so the CUDA build from PyPI (~8 GB of NVIDIA libraries) can't be
# picked by accident. macOS wheels on PyPI are already CPU-only.
torch==2.15.0+cpu ; sys_platform == "linux"   # >= 2.6.0 for CVE-2025-32434
torch==2.15.0 ; sys_platform == "darwin"
transformers>=5.10.0        # CVE-2023-6730 and later deserialization/RCE advisories
